# NEVER commit firmware or firmware-derived blobs. This project distributes NO firmware.
# Bring your own FwPkt; keep it out of the repo.
FwPkt/
FwPkt*.zip
*.ubifs
*.bin
uImage
config
firmwareInfo
crcInfo

# Build inputs/outputs
in/
out/
work/
build/
*.so
pgphoto*
ptp2*
appfs*
*.img

# ...but DO track the source files shipped inside the container image that the
# broad build-artifact patterns above would otherwise swallow. These are the
# author's own scripts/wrapper (NOT built binaries) and must be in the repo or a
# fresh clone cannot build the image.
!container/ondisk/pgphoto.wrapper.in

# Toolchain source cache
src/libgphoto2-*/
*.tar.xz
*.tar.bz2
*.tar.gz

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# LM Studio bridge conversation ledger (append-only, grows ~100 KB per review;
# rotated reviews live in docs/evidence/ledger-archive-*.md which IS tracked)
LMStudioLogEnhancements.md

# Session workspace state (rebuilt every session; never authoritative).
# Per issue #30, this is a per-session scratch file for the agent host, not
# repo content; the canonical FwPkt-install investigation log lives in the
# dedicated analysis repo (issue #17 split).
STATE.md

# Per-host build outputs from container runs (out/<date>-<flavour>/). The
# FwPkt inputs the user supplied are NOT here — those live under FwPkt/
# (already ignored). `out/` is the container-side mirror.
#
# Per issue #30, `builds/` is load-bearing for provenance claims (see
# issues #3/#7 which reference builds/…/build-source-provenance.txt). The
# compromise: ignore the directory at root so `git status` stays clean, but
# anyone reproducing a build can rebuild the same provenance locally and
# compare hashes. Provenance itself is *not* tracked.
builds/

# Cross-project coordination notes (see docs/CROSS-PROJECT.md for the
# rationale; that file is the public-facing version of this convention).
# Excluded from this repo, not deleted.
docs/CROSS-PROJECT.md
